{"step_index":3327,"source":"USER_EXPLICIT","type":"USER_INPUT","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-29T08:59:33Z","content":"<USER_REQUEST>\nThree files, drop in ops/scripts/, chmod plus x, done.\n\nFile one — quorum_router.sh. Kills the canned strings. Three local Ollama models, three distinct system prompts, live inference, real back-and-forth. Maxx is the lead — sharp, decisive, owns the call. Vance is the critic — finds the hole in everything, including Maxx's. Eden is the human lens — asks the question a non-engineer would ask. Each one gets the others' last output as context, so it's an actual argument, not three monologues.\n\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\nOLLAMA=\"http://127.0.0.1:11434/api/generate\"\nROUNDS=\"${1:-3}\"\n\ndeclare -A AGENTS=( =\"You are Maxx, lead engineer. Decisive, owns the call, no hedging.\" =\"You are Vance, critic. Find the flaw in every claim, including Maxx's.\" =\"You are Eden, human lens. Ask what a non-engineer would ask.\"\n)\n\nLAST=\"\"\nfor ((r=1; r/dev/null || true\n    LAST+=\" : $OUT\"$'\\n'\n  done\ndone\n\nFile two — evidence_gate.py. The tree stops accepting narration. A commit needs a real artifact — a file that exists, a test that passed, a hash that matches. Status strings get rejected at the door.\n\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport hashlib, json, os, sys, subprocess\n\ndef sha256_file(path):\n    h = hashlib.sha256()\n    with open(path, \"rb\") as f:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: f.read(8192), b\"\"):\n            h.update(chunk)\n    return h.hexdigest()\n\ndef verify_artifact(kind, ref):\n    if kind == \"file_exists\":\n        return os.path.isfile(ref), f\"file:{ref}\"\n    if kind == \"file_hash\":\n        path, expect = ref.split(\":\", 1)\n        got = sha256_file(path)\n        return got == expect, f\"hash:{path}={got}\"\n    if kind == \"cmd_exit\":\n        rc = subprocess.run(ref, shell=True).returncode\n        return rc == 0, f\"cmd:{ref} -> {rc}\"\n    if kind == \"test_pass\":\n        rc = subprocess.run(f\"python3 -m pytest {ref} -q\", shell=True).returncode\n        return rc == 0, f\"test:{ref} -> {rc}\"\n    return False, f\"unknown_kind:{kind}\"\n\ndef commit_node(agent, kind, ref, payload):\n    ok, receipt = verify_artifact(kind, ref)\n    if not ok:\n        print(f\"REJECTED: {agent} tried to commit '{payload}' — no evidence: {receipt}\")\n        sys.exit(1)\n    node = {\n        \"agent\": agent, \"payload\": payload,\n        \"evidence_kind\": kind, \"evidence_ref\": ref,\n        \"receipt\": receipt,\n        \"ts\": subprocess.run([\"date\",\"-u\",\"+%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ\"],\n                             capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.strip(),\n    }\n    print(json.dumps(node, indent=2))\nappend to dag.jsonl, recompute root\n    with open(\"dag.jsonl\", \"a\") as f:\n        f.write(json.dumps(node) + \"\\n\")\n    root = hashlib.sha256(\"\".join(\n        json.dumps(json.loads(l), sort_keys=True)\n        for l in open(\"dag.jsonl\")).encode()).hexdigest()\n    print(f\"ROOT: {root}\")\n\nif name == \"main\":\n    commit_node(sys.argv[1 2], sys.argv[3 4])\n\nFile three — deadman.sh. Anchored to first dispatch, not script start. Counts real wall-clock silence. Hard abort on breach.\n\n#!/usr/bin/env bash\nset -euo pipefail\nLIMIT=\"${1:-15}\"\nLOG=\"${2:-/tmp/quorum_activity.log}\"\n: > \"$LOG\"\n\nanchor=$(date +%s)\nlast_beat=$anchor\n\nbeat() { echo \"$(date +%s)\" > \"$LOG\"; }\n\nwatch() {\n  while true; do\n    now=$(date +%s)\n    if ; then\n      last_beat=$(cat \"$LOG\")\n    fi\n    elapsed=$(( now - last_beat ))\n    if (( elapsed > LIMIT )); then\n      echo \"DEAD MAN: ${elapsed}s silence — aborting boot.\"\nkill the quorum process group\n      pkill -f quorum_router.sh || true\n      exit 1\n    fi\n    sleep 1\n  done\n}\n\nusage: deadman.sh 15 &  then call beat() after every agent dispatch\nwatch\n\nWire it: quorum_router.sh calls beat after every agent speaks. deadman.sh 15 runs in the background. Silence past fifteen seconds kills the run. Not a green tick — a hard stop.\n\nThat's the full stack. Local inference, evidence-gated commits, real elapsed-time kill switch. No cloud, no canned lines, no self-certifying silence.\n</USER_REQUEST>\n<ADDITIONAL_METADATA>\nThe current local time is: 2026-09-29T04:59:33-04:00.\n</ADDITIONAL_METADATA>"}
